@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/class-diagram
!theme spacelab

title Device Composable Behaviors — Polling & State

interface Device {
}
note right of Device
  Defined in 04 Device Contract.
end note

interface Polling {
  +interval(): Duration
  +pollOnce(): CompletableFuture<Response<Void>>
  +startPolling(executor: ScheduledExecutorService): void
  +stopPolling(): void
}
note right of Polling
  Composable behavior, not a forced base class.
  startPolling() is a default method that wires a
  repeating call to pollOnce(); a device only
  implements this if it actually polls. On failure:
  mark stopped + record triggered rule (START_FAILURE).
  Uses a CommunicationClient internally — never a
  protocol-specific type (see 01 Communication
  Client Core).
end note

interface StatefulDevice {
  +stateManager(): StateManager
}
note right of StatefulDevice
  Composable behavior for devices that track
  operational state + triggered rules. A device
  implements this only if it needs state tracking.
end note

class StateManager {
  +updateState(operational: Map, triggeredRules: Map): void
}

class BlaubergMVHR {}
note bottom of BlaubergMVHR
  Composes only the behaviors it needs:
  Device + Polling + StatefulDevice. A future
  event-driven (non-polling) device would
  implement Device (+ StatefulDevice if needed)
  and simply skip Polling. Defined in full in
  06 Example Device Extensions.
end note

BlaubergMVHR ..|> Device
BlaubergMVHR ..|> Polling
BlaubergMVHR ..|> StatefulDevice
BlaubergMVHR -- StateManager

@enduml
